2026-11-18 20:47:46 - Agent_20261118204404 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL findings for unsafe deserialization vulnerabilities (CWE-502) in Jinja2 bytecode cache. Identified and submitted 2 true positive findings:

1. Line 73 (src/jinja2/bccache.py): Unsafe pickle.load() deserialization of checksum data from file object
2. Line 79 (src/jinja2/bccache.py): Unsafe marshal.load() deserialization of bytecode from file object

Both vulnerabilities allow arbitrary code execution if an attacker can control the cached bytecode files. The attack surface includes:
- FileSystemBytecodeCache: Reads from filesystem cache files
- DirectoryBytecodeCache: Reads from directory-based cache files
- bytecode_from_string(): Accepts arbitrary bytes and deserializes them

The vulnerabilities are mitigated by magic header validation and checksum verification, but these are insufficient against determined attackers who can write to cache directories.
